FAQs
Q: What if the caller can't confirm at least 2 of the 4 identity items?
Do not issue a reset. Escalate to your team lead, or ask the requester to retry self-service once they regain access to a verified phone or email.
Q: Why doesn't this flow send a verification code the way self-service does?
The self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.

